    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9829" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">concinnātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id. (post-class.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In
			economics, <i>an adjusting, preparing</i>: aquae
			marinae, Auct. Lemmat. ap. <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R.
			106</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a making,
			composing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">epistulae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 17</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 7</span></i> and 15:
			metrorum, Mar. Vict. p. 2547 P.</div>
